@startuml
title UC08 Conduct Consultation and Record Clinical Information — black-box SSD
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 350
hide footbox
actor "Authorised treating\nhealthcare professional" as Actor
participant "Appointment Tracking System\n(black box)" as System

note over Actor, System
  UC08 steps 1–7. A selected appointment/patient context already exists.
  Session actor is implicit. Recording rechecks treating authority, confirmed + arrived
  state, clinical-record consistency, valid content and absence of an existing consultation.
end note

Actor -> System : viewClinicalRecord(patientID)
alt record absent, role/care access denied or required read audit unavailable
  break Clinical lookup failed — no recording or optional actions follow
    System --> Actor : safe failure; no clinical content; denial audited when applicable
  end
else clinical access permitted and sensitive-read audit retained
  System --> Actor : authorised clinical record view
end
note over Actor
  Conduct consultation with patient outside the system;
  prepare observations, diagnoses, treatment
  recommendations and follow-up requirements.
end note

Actor -> System : recordConsultation(appointmentID,observations,diagnoses,treatmentRecommendations,followUpRequirements)
alt authority/state/record consistency/content invalid OR consultation already exists
  break Recording rejected — no prescription or follow-up may follow in this attempt
    System --> Actor : safe failure; no consultation, record addition or completion\n(denied action audited without clinical content)
  end
else write or required audit retention fails
  break Recording not committed
    System --> Actor : recording failure; no consultation, record addition or completion
  end
else all recording checks and persistence succeed
  System --> Actor : consultationID, completed\n(consultation linked to patient's clinical record; arrival preserved)
end

note over Actor, System
  Core UC08 has succeeded. Optional actions below are independent writes:
  their failure must not undo the recorded consultation or completed appointment.
end note

opt prescription clinically indicated — UC10 / UC08 extension 7a
  Actor -> System : issuePrescription(consultationID,items)
  alt care/prescribing authority denied OR items empty/incomplete OR medication invalid
    System --> Actor : prescription rejected; no prescription or partial items\n(core consultation remains recorded)
  else prescription write or required audit retention fails
    System --> Actor : prescription failed; no prescription or partial items
  else permitted, >= 1 complete medication/dosage/instructions item, write audited
    System --> Actor : prescriptionID linked to consultation\n(no electronic pharmacy transmission)
  end
end

opt follow-up clinically indicated — UC11 / UC08 extension 7b
  alt actor searches availability first
    Actor -> System : searchAvailability(serviceID, professionalID, locationID, dateRange)
    alt invalid/denied search or no candidate intervals
      break End this follow-up attempt — requestFollowUp cannot follow failed search
        System --> Actor : safe failure / no availability; no follow-up reservation\n(core consultation remains recorded)
      end
    else candidate intervals exist
      System --> Actor : candidate start times and duration; no reservation
    end
  else valid candidate already selected
    note over Actor, System
      Availability search is optional; requestFollowUp always
      revalidates the full interval and required/supplied referral.
    end note
  end
  Actor -> System : requestFollowUp(consultationID,serviceID,professionalID,locationID,startTime,referralID?)
  alt care authority denied, slot/offering/overlap invalid OR referral missing/unusable/mismatched
    System --> Actor : safe follow-up failure; no appointment or reservation\n(core consultation remains recorded)
  else follow-up write or required audit retention fails
    System --> Actor : follow-up failed; no appointment, origin link or reservation
  else same scheduling/referral rules as requestAppointment pass; write audited
    System --> Actor : follow-up appointmentID, requested\n(slot reserved; linked to consultation; patient derived from consultation)
  end
end

note over Actor, System
  Follow-up is not automatically confirmed. All sensitive reads, successful writes and
  denied actions retain safe audit metadata, never narrative or medication details.
  UC08 extensions 1a/2a, 4a/5a, 5b, 6a, 7a/7a.1, 7b/7b.1/7b.2 and 7c.
end note
@enduml
